# What the image build is allowed to see.
#
# An allowlist, not a list of things to forget. The denylist version of this file
# is correct on the day it is written and wrong the first time somebody adds a
# directory: `web/node_modules` alone is 460 MB, `.git` is the whole history, and
# a local library or a `curator.db` carrying an encrypted WireGuard key would
# otherwise be uploaded to the daemon on every build and land in a layer.
#
# So: exclude everything, then name the five things three build stages read.
# Adding a source directory to this repo means adding a line here, which is the
# failure mode we want — a build that cannot find a file, rather than a build
# that quietly ships one.

*

!cmd
!internal
!web
!go.mod
!go.sum

# The `ffmpeg` stage runs this one file, and nothing else in scripts/ is part of
# an image build (docs/tasks/T47-image.md). scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh reads it out
# of the same context, so the path is load-bearing in two places.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/ffmpeg.sh

# The 460 MB, and the two generated trees beside it. The `ui` stage runs
# `npm ci` from the lockfile, so a local node_modules is not only large, it is
# the wrong one — it was installed for darwin/arm64.
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/out

# The UI export is NOT copied in from the working tree: the `ui` stage builds it
# and the `build` stage takes it from there. Shipping whatever happened to be in
# dist/ is how an image gets a UI three commits older than its binary, and the
# symptom is a screen that is merely missing a button (docs/decisions.md D16).
internal/web/dist

# Fixtures. 29 folders the parser meets in tests and nothing in the image reads.
testdata
internal/*/testdata

# Anything a `go run` in the working tree leaves behind. The database and its key
# are the ones that matter: DB_PATH defaults to ./curator.db, the key is written
# beside it, and together they are the settings store with the WireGuard private
# key in it (docs/decisions.md D28).
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
curator.key
.env
.env.*
downloads
